L0210: Field does not exist

The receiver type has no field with this name or position. Tuple field names bind dependencies inside the type but do not create named accessors; access tuple components positionally or destructure them. Struct field access uses the actual declared field labels.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/field_of_a_tuple_by_name.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```rust
// A tuple is projected by position.
fn first(pair: (u8, u8)) -> u8 {
    pair.left
}
```

Language, as built: [1.3:2](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.3:2).
